+/*
+ * The cooperative timer, and the only asynchronous entry this guest has.
+ *
+ * Declared unconditionally: a cooperative kernel is one built from this tree,
+ * and the entry costs nothing when co_colinux_guest is false because nothing
+ * ever jumps to it. There is no IDT gate -- the host synthesises the entry by
+ * pointing its resume at asm_sysvec_co_timer over a frame it builds itself, so
+ * what runs afterwards is the stock idtentry body: error_entry decides swapgs
+ * from the interrupted CS, and irqentry_exit does the preemption and the
+ * return-to-user work. That reuse is the point. Every part of delivering an
+ * interrupt that is easy to get wrong is already written and tested here.
