+ * it with Windows; spinning here holds that core away from the host for up to
+ * the poll window, and whatever that costs exceeds the crossing it avoids.
+ *
+ * So the cadence has to be fixed without the guest holding the processor --
+ * the host must re-enter promptly when a completion is published, rather than
+ * the guest waiting for it to. That is a monitor-side change, and note that the
+ * obvious monitor-side version has also already failed: re-entering up to 64
+ * times per idle kept the pinned core crossing under cli and starved the very
+ * daemon that answers the fence (see the note in switch.c).
