+	 * irq_enter() is not bookkeeping. current is the idle task and this is
+	 * the outermost count, so it takes the is_idle_task() branch into
+	 * tick_irq_enter() -- ktime_get(), and tick_do_update_jiffies64() under
+	 * jiffies_lock -- and ct_irq_enter() suspends the RCU extended
+	 * quiescent state that default_idle_call() established one frame up.
+	 * irq_exit() then runs whatever softirqs that raised. Around an EMPTY
+	 * drain, all of it runs and none of it is wanted.
+	 *
+	 * And on the boot processor it is always empty until smp_init(): the
+	 * only writers of this bitmap are co_colinux_ipi_send() and the
