+		 * first moment anything can post into this processor's own set.
+		 * That is the gate working and the mechanism still being lethal,
+		 * not the mechanism being fixed.
+		 *
+		 * irq_enter() is the suspect half: current is the idle task and
+		 * this is the outermost count, so it takes the is_idle_task()
+		 * branch into tick_irq_enter() -- ktime_get() and
+		 * tick_do_update_jiffies64() under jiffies_lock -- and
+		 * ct_irq_enter() suspends the RCU extended quiescent state that
+		 * default_idle_call() established one frame up. irq_exit() then
+		 * runs whatever softirqs that raised.
+		 *
+		 * Interrupts are already disabled here, so the dispatched
+		 * handlers keep that much of their contract; what they lose is
+		 * in_interrupt(), which may WARN. A WARN the host steps over is
+		 * a result. A reset is not.
+		 *
+		 * BISECT CONCLUDED, and it proved nothing -- restored.
+		 *
+		 * While no secondary existed this set was always empty, so the
+		 * gated block never executed in either build. That is why
